I didn't create a plugin because on further inspection it might not be neccesary to set the names on each request, though in my system I have the configuration that was quoted above.

Since the change in configuration from some versions ago, you can just try to import newrelic in top of nuxt.config.js.

And if you need further customization, use a hook like

```
hooks: {
    'render:route' (url, result, context) {
      try {
        newrelic.setTransactionName(url)
      } catch (error) {
        // Ignore
      }
    }
  }
```

